00:01:39.110 --> 00:01:41.567
things that I observed, what
you can do to improve them,

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:43.590
and I believe these are really interesting

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.950
and helpful insights
for all of you as well,

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:47.880
things that you should all take care of,

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.250
things that you should look out for

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.520
when you create your
CVs, and many of these

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:53.220
are things that I see
frequently done wrong

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.190
by many people, so I hope and trust

00:01:55.190 --> 00:01:56.900
that this is really going to be valuable

00:01:56.900 --> 00:01:58.027
and interesting to all of you.

00:01:58.027 --> 00:02:00.673
And to start it off it is
important for me to say

00:02:00.673 --> 00:02:03.500
that all the remarks and
the things that I will say,

00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:05.500
and critique, and give you as a feedback,

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.250
these are my opinions.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:11.160
I do not claim that I know
the truth about how a perfect

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:13.400
CV looks like, there are
many opinions on that,

00:02:13.400 --> 00:02:15.130
and maybe if you ask other people

00:02:15.130 --> 00:02:16.380
they will give you another opinion.

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.240
But hey, you asked me, this is my channel,

00:02:18.240 --> 00:02:19.930
so my opinion is what you will get.

00:02:19.930 --> 00:02:22.240
And as always, take it
with a grain of salt,

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:24.540
and in the end it's important
that you are comfortable

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:26.120
with your application material,

00:02:26.120 --> 00:02:27.780
and if you have a good reason to deviate

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:29.930
from what I'm telling
you, then of course do so.

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:32.460
So let's go briefly into
some general remarks

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.000
about the CV structure.

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:36.160
One thing that I would
strongly recommend to you

00:02:36.160 --> 00:02:37.890
is to have a one-pager format.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:42.120
The one-pager CV is just
so much easier to read

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:44.320
and comprehend than a two-pager CV.

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.387
Especially in Anglo-Saxon
countries, one-pager CVs

00:02:47.387 --> 00:02:49.105
are the standard, they are the norm,

00:02:49.105 --> 00:02:50.680
and there you really should apply

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:51.950
with a one-pager CV.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:54.830
In some countries, such
as Germany, two-pager CVs

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.780
are generally accepted as
well, but as a general rule

00:02:57.780 --> 00:02:59.850
you should never go over two pages,

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:01.820
and in general, I highly encourage you,

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.310
even in Germany, to go for the one-pager,

00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.940
it is always much better,
I love it when I get

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:08.600
a one-pager CV on my desk.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:11.220
In my humble opinion it just
looks much more professional,

00:03:11.220 --> 00:03:13.860
and it's much easier for
you to communicate yourself

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.160
on the one-pager format.

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.410
And from the CVs that
you sent me some are on

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:19.370
a two-pager format, and on these examples

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:21.620
I will try to give you some
hints on what you can cut

00:03:21.620 --> 00:03:23.697
down to get it down to a one-pager.

00:03:23.697 --> 00:03:25.380
Now let's look into the content blocks,

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.100
what are the key content
blocks that your CV

00:03:28.100 --> 00:03:29.760
should consist of, and in the structure

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:32.420
that I will propose here,
there are three main

00:03:32.420 --> 00:03:35.340
content blocks and then
two minor content blocks

00:03:35.340 --> 00:03:36.350
in the footer.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:39.530
And I prepared a very basic
template of these different

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:42.600
content blocks that you have,
just as a rough guideline.

00:03:42.600 --> 00:03:45.360
At the very top you should
have your personal information,

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.800
your contact information,
so state your name,

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.290
your address, your email,
your telephone number,

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:53.070
and so on, this'll make it
easy for the company to contact

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:54.540
you without needing to look up other

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:55.940
application material of yours.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:58.830
Then the three main
content blocks are first

00:03:58.830 --> 00:04:01.860
your professional experience,
second your education,

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:03.890
and third your extracurriculars.

00:04:03.890 --> 00:04:06.240
So in your professional
experience this is where you list

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:08.970
all your jobs, internships,
and similar things.

00:04:08.970 --> 00:04:11.810
In your education you list
all the degrees that you have,

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.420
the universities that you attended.

00:04:13.420 --> 00:04:15.700
In the extracurriculars
you especially list

00:04:15.700 --> 00:04:17.810
all the social things
that you did, so any kind

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:20.610
of volunteering that you
did, nonprofit organizations

00:04:20.610 --> 00:04:22.660
where you had some kind of
leadership positions in,

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:23.773
and similar things like that.

00:04:23.773 --> 00:04:26.300
Then you have honors and awards
section where you can list

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:29.830
all your academic achievements,
prizes, scholarships,

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:31.867
dean list positions, and
anything similar like that

00:04:31.867 --> 00:04:33.700
that will make you stand out.

00:04:33.700 --> 00:04:35.757
And in the end you have an
other qualifications section

00:04:35.757 --> 00:04:38.220
where you can list all
your language skills,

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:41.030
IT skills, any other
certificates that you get,

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:43.050
and similar things that
you might want to highlight

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.700
to your potential future employer.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:46.507
So of course this is
just a rough structure,

00:04:46.507 --> 00:04:49.840
and you can debate how exactly
the wording of these headers

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:51.730
should be, you can debate
whether you should add

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:54.770
an additional line for
hobbies at the very bottom,

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.140
but generally speaking
if you follow a structure

00:04:57.140 --> 00:05:00.020
like that then your overall
structure should be fine.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:02.910
And now when reviewing the
individual CVs I will often

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.130
refer back to this structure,
so have this in mind,

00:05:05.130 --> 00:05:06.980
this is the basic recommended structure

00:05:06.980 --> 00:05:07.960
that I will refer to.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.340
So without further ado,
let's jump into it,

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:12.627
let's get practical and
review the first CV.

00:05:12.627 --> 00:05:14.800
And the first thing I'd like to address

00:05:14.800 --> 00:05:16.190
is the one-pager format.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:18.890
So as you can easily see
this CV is on a two-pager

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:21.000
format, and I just wanna address the point

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:23.700
that many of you are saying,
"Well I just cannot fit this

00:05:23.700 --> 00:05:24.690
on a one-pager."

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.130
But I'm telling you,
you can absolutely fit

00:05:27.130 --> 00:05:29.130
such a CV on a one-pager format.

00:05:29.130 --> 00:05:31.120
So let's just go over couple of things

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:33.037
this guy could do to
get it on a one-pager.

00:05:33.037 --> 00:05:35.500
And the first is the header of the CV,

00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.963
with all the contact information.

00:05:36.963 --> 00:05:39.730
Here just so much space
is wasted on a header,

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:42.130
all the information here
could just easily be

00:05:42.130 --> 00:05:45.490
included in two lines or so,
and we will see other CVs

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:48.770
in this set of four CV
where this has been done.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:51.080
So for your header don't
put each individual

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:53.040
item of information in one new line,

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:55.570
but have them all in one
line after each other,

00:05:55.570 --> 00:05:57.090
and this is absolutely fine.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:05:58.850
Next is the borders at the sides.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:00.860
He has a significant margin to the left

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.960
and to the right, and if
you will just take out

00:06:02.960 --> 00:06:04.780
a bit of the margin he
probably wouldn't need

00:06:04.780 --> 00:06:07.180
some of the text breaks, and
some of the bullet points,

00:06:07.180 --> 00:06:09.340
so you would save a
whole line by doing that.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.970
Same is true for the
spacing between the dates

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:13.960
and the text, there's just so much space

00:06:13.960 --> 00:06:16.320
between the date and the
text, if you would just let

00:06:16.320 --> 00:06:19.457
the text start a bit more to
the left you would save space

00:06:19.457 --> 00:06:22.350
and probably save several
lines in the indentation.

00:06:22.350 --> 00:06:24.500
Before we now dive into
the content let's go over

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:27.000
some other minor format and layout things

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.450
which I would recommend to improve.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:30.070
So first regarding the date range,

00:06:30.070 --> 00:06:31.970
whenever you write something that is still

00:06:31.970 --> 00:06:34.520
an ongoing activity, the way he puts it

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.577
with a dash and then nothing after that

00:06:36.577 --> 00:06:39.080
is a bit weird, I would
probably not do it like this.

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:41.750
Instead I would just write
"since" and then the date,

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:44.090
without this empty dash afterwards.

00:06:44.090 --> 00:06:47.270
Then the font that he is using
looks a bit informal to me,

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:48.990
so I'm not exactly sure
which font that is,

00:06:48.990 --> 00:06:51.550
probably something similar
to Calibri, but at least

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:54.100
for my taste it looks a bit
too playful and informal,

00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:55.400
so I'd probably go for another one.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.087
And just a little minor
thing on the bottom right

00:06:57.087 --> 00:06:59.270
you see that he still wrote
(speaking foreign language),

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:02.100
so this is German for page,
so of course if you have

00:07:02.100 --> 00:07:04.230
different versions of your
CVs in different languages

00:07:04.230 --> 00:07:06.610
please make sure that you
translate every single word.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.420
This is just a small
inaccuracy that of course

00:07:08.420 --> 00:07:09.253
should be avoided.

00:07:09.253 --> 00:07:10.497
Now let's dive into the content

00:07:10.497 --> 00:07:12.870
and let's start with
the education section.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.770
What you see here that
this guy did some kind

00:07:14.770 --> 00:07:17.440
of a computer science degree,
and probably especially if

00:07:17.440 --> 00:07:19.700
you're fresh out of
university with your degree

00:07:19.700 --> 00:07:22.660
I'd also try to highlight
your area of specialization,

00:07:22.660 --> 00:07:25.300
all of the focus fields that
you did during your studies,

00:07:25.300 --> 00:07:27.377
and of course if you
apply for a specific job

00:07:27.377 --> 00:07:29.910
I'd try to tailor it a
bit that it really fits

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:31.200
the content of the job.

00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:33.210
So for instance, if you
apply for a finance position

00:07:33.210 --> 00:07:34.640
try to tailor what you write here,

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.050
your areas of specialization
towards that role,

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:38.970
highlight the finance
courses that you did.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:41.120
And regarding grades, yes
it's correct you should always

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:42.640
put your grades on the CV.

00:07:42.640 --> 00:07:44.540
Two tips that I would
have to maybe improve

00:07:44.540 --> 00:07:46.480
the appearance of your
grade is that first,

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:49.024
whenever it makes sense for
you to name the percentile

00:07:49.024 --> 00:07:50.187
of your grade, do it.

00:07:50.187 --> 00:07:53.770
So here on this grade, 2.18
is of course an okayish grade,

00:07:53.770 --> 00:07:56.370
but maybe you're studying in
a very tough degree subject,

00:07:56.370 --> 00:07:59.960
maybe he's already in the top
10% or top 15% of performers

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:01.520
of his class with that grade.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:03.220
So I do not know how in computer science

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:05.610
the grade distribution looks
like, but if you can make

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:08.640
such a claim, that you are
in the top 10% of your class

00:08:08.640 --> 00:08:10.930
it's of course highly beneficial,
and then I would really

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:13.310
recommend you to add that
to your grade section.

00:08:13.310 --> 00:08:14.403
Another advice is with your thesis,

00:08:14.403 --> 00:08:17.060
so with your bachelor
thesis or master thesis,

00:08:17.060 --> 00:08:18.758
if you have achieved
a grade in your thesis

00:08:18.758 --> 00:08:21.010
that is significantly
better than the overall

00:08:21.010 --> 00:08:23.330
GPA of your degree,
then I would add the GPA

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:26.460
of the thesis as well in
brackets after the normal grade.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:28.320
Regarding the exchange
semester that this guy did,

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:30.170
I believe it takes far too much space,

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:32.730
especially in comparison
to the main degrees

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:33.800
that he's actually doing.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.920
So for the exchange
semester I'd put all of this

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:38.240
only one line, by this you save one line

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.460
and could potentially invest
it in going into more detail

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:42.320
on what you did in your main degree.

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.180
Now to the work experience section,

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:46.630
and here I would encourage
you to whenever possible

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.870
use parallel grammar structures.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:51.120
And what this means is that
from a grammar point of view

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:53.800
you start all your
bullets in the same way.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.350
And you see this nicely
done at his Suzuki entry

00:08:56.350 --> 00:08:59.000
where he started both of
the bullets with a verb,

00:08:59.000 --> 00:09:00.950
and usually for the
work experience section

00:09:00.950 --> 00:09:03.580
it's good and advised to
start with such a verb,

00:09:03.580 --> 00:09:05.810
because this now emphasizes
more on what you did,

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:07.417
what you actually did at these positions,

00:09:07.417 --> 00:09:09.150
and this is always what you want.

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:10.760
If you have bullets which are all written

00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:12.630
in the parallel grammar structure,

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:13.840
it's just much easier to understand,

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:16.230
much more effortless to read,
it just gives an overall

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:17.660
much more professional appearance.

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:19.157
Now the next thing on the work experience,

00:09:19.157 --> 00:09:21.810
and this might be the
most important point,

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.860
because this is a feedback
point that I will need to give

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:25.320
to every single CV.

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:27.770
In the bullets describing
your work experience,

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.920
you should focus on the
impact, you should focus

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.050
on what you have achieved,
and not only as a team

00:09:34.050 --> 00:09:38.130
but what your contribution
to a specific point was.

00:09:38.130 --> 00:09:40.230
What I mean by that is
that you should not just

00:09:40.230 --> 00:09:43.180
write a couple of general
buzz words describing

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.530
the activities on a
superficial level such as

00:09:45.530 --> 00:09:47.910
first level support, but
you should rather say

00:09:47.910 --> 00:09:50.490
exactly and specifically what you did

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:53.410
and what your impact was,
and whenever possible

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.270
also to quantify that.

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:57.327
So just a little example,
instead of writing

00:09:57.327 --> 00:10:00.847
"first level support", you
can write something like

00:10:00.847 --> 00:10:03.387
"Responsible for first level support

00:10:03.387 --> 00:10:05.720
"of thousand employees, comma,

00:10:05.720 --> 00:10:08.930
resolving 50 plus tickets everyday."

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:10.760
Now this sounds much more like impact,

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:12.880
if I read it as somebody who gets the CV

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.640
I can imagine much more
what you actually did

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:17.770
than just by reading first level support,

00:10:17.770 --> 00:10:19.570
because this can mean
everything and nothing.

00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:22.190
Another example here for the PwC position,

00:10:22.190 --> 00:10:24.840
if you talk about a role
out of a monitoring tool,

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:26.050
try to give a bit more detail,

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:29.080
what exactly did you do and
how can you quantify that?

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:32.730
So for instance, say how many
users actually used your tool.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.750
So if you can claim that
you as a working student

00:10:34.750 --> 00:10:38.130
created a tool that afterwards
hundreds of consultants

00:10:38.130 --> 00:10:41.840
used at PWC, of course that
is extremely impressive.

00:10:41.840 --> 00:10:44.410
So add a bit more flavor,
or say specifically

00:10:44.410 --> 00:10:46.920
what you did, what your contribution was,

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:49.120
what the impact was that you delivered,

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.030
and also make it quantified.

00:10:51.030 --> 00:10:53.920
This is really what
distinguishes a strong framing

00:10:53.920 --> 00:10:55.800
of work experience from a weak one.

00:10:55.800 --> 00:10:57.500
The next point of observation that I have,

00:10:57.500 --> 00:10:59.320
but I also see other people doing wrong,

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.810
is that you do not need
to give equal weight,

00:11:01.810 --> 00:11:03.330
equal space in your CV

00:11:03.330 --> 00:11:05.110
to every single individual position.

00:11:05.110 --> 00:11:07.010
So in this specific example the position

00:11:07.010 --> 00:11:08.500
that you had as a student assistant,

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:10.840
at the Hessisches
Landesmuseum, probably is a bit

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:12.970
less relevant, it's a bit less impressive

00:11:12.970 --> 00:11:14.930
for the most jobs that you will apply to,

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:17.450
compared to for instance
your PwC position.

00:11:17.450 --> 00:11:19.740
So I'd already give more space in your CV

00:11:19.740 --> 00:11:21.460
to the things that are really important

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:23.430
and relevant, and less space to the things

00:11:23.430 --> 00:11:24.520
that are less relevant.

00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:26.820
And at some point if you've
collected now even more

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:29.290
internships, maybe even
already have a job,

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:31.570
at some point you can also start dropping

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:33.610
these less important
positions that you have.

00:11:33.610 --> 00:11:36.030
You do not need to list
every single internship

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:37.490
that you did during your studies.

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:39.930
And just as example also, for me on my CV,

00:11:39.930 --> 00:11:41.860
even though I did all kinds of internship

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:44.640
during my university times,
most of them I just do not

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:46.890
list anymore on my CV
because now of course

00:11:46.890 --> 00:11:49.600
I like to emphasize far more
the actual full-time work

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:51.750
experience that I got after graduating.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:54.280
Now regarding the qualifications
and skills sections,

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:56.330
the first suggestion that
I would have is to put

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:58.900
this behind, below the
volunteering section.

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:00.750
So as I've shown you
in my overall template

00:12:00.750 --> 00:12:02.760
I believe it's common
practice to rather start

00:12:02.760 --> 00:12:04.790
with your extracurriculars,
with your volunteering,

00:12:04.790 --> 00:12:07.057
and then start with the
qualifications and skills.

00:12:07.057 --> 00:12:09.820
Now here if I look into the
qualifications and skills here

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:12.430
I believe there's lots of
opportunities to cut down

00:12:12.430 --> 00:12:13.540
space as well.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:15.540
So for the language there's just no need

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:17.760
to put languages in individual lines,

00:12:17.760 --> 00:12:20.160
you can just write them
in one line, one language

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:20.993
after each other.

00:12:20.993 --> 00:12:23.940
So languages, and then German,
English, Russian, French,

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:25.540
with the proficiency level in brackets

00:12:25.540 --> 00:12:27.300
is completely fine, it will
just take you one line.

00:12:27.300 --> 00:12:29.770
And then next regarding
software and tools,

00:12:29.770 --> 00:12:32.150
and I know many people do
that, but from my perspective

00:12:32.150 --> 00:12:34.360
there's no need at all to write about

00:12:34.360 --> 00:12:36.090
your Microsoft Office skills.

00:12:36.090 --> 00:12:38.250
If you're a master
graduate from a university

00:12:38.250 --> 00:12:40.780
people will just assume that
you have basic office skills,

00:12:40.780 --> 00:12:42.830
exception might be if
you have really in depth

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:45.330
knowledge on specific
fields, for instance VBA,

00:12:45.330 --> 00:12:47.100
then yes you can put
this, but just writing

00:12:47.100 --> 00:12:49.350
about Microsoft Office in
general is not something

00:12:49.350 --> 00:12:50.980
I would do, it's just a waste of space.

00:12:50.980 --> 00:12:52.730
And the very same is true for Windows.

00:12:52.730 --> 00:12:54.170
I mean, come on, people will just know,

00:12:54.170 --> 00:12:55.760
expect you, and trust
you that you will have

00:12:55.760 --> 00:12:58.270
basic knowledge of Windows,
there's no need of writing that.

00:12:58.270 --> 00:12:59.630
And here there is a distinction between

00:12:59.630 --> 00:13:02.230
software and the programming,
frankly here I also believe

00:13:02.230 --> 00:13:03.590
that this is just a waste of space,

00:13:03.590 --> 00:13:05.110
you can consolidate this much more.

00:13:05.110 --> 00:13:06.960
So for instance, yeah I'm not an expert

00:13:06.960 --> 00:13:09.340
but at least based on, I
know Anaconda and Spyder

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:12.140
are IDEs for Python, so
it's completely sufficient

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:14.350
to just say that you are
proficient in Python.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.290
There's no need now to
also mention all the IDEs

00:13:16.290 --> 00:13:18.360
that you have worked with in the past.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.920
Maybe this might be a bit more different

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:22.110
if you really apply
for a computer science,

00:13:22.110 --> 00:13:23.247
for a software developer position

00:13:23.247 --> 00:13:24.890
and you know that these are the things

00:13:24.890 --> 00:13:27.470
that are going to be used there,
but for a general business

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:30.080
position there's no need into
going this much of detail.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.110
Same is true for R and R Studio,

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:33.530
you do not need to mention
that you're proficient

00:13:33.530 --> 00:13:35.167
in R Studio if you're proficient in R,

00:13:35.167 --> 00:13:37.510
I mean this is pretty
much self explanatory.

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:39.620
So bottom line here
again from my perspective

00:13:39.620 --> 00:13:41.630
you can consolidate this whole section

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:44.410
in just one line under
the title of IT skills,

00:13:44.410 --> 00:13:46.600
or something like that, and
then just list all of these

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:48.240
things, then you should be completely.

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:51.700
Now regarding the volunteering
section, and here would focus

00:13:51.700 --> 00:13:54.980
much more on impact, on your leadership,

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.350
and focusing on mentioning
as many things as possible.

00:13:57.350 --> 00:13:59.890
What people will look for,
if they read these CVs

00:13:59.890 --> 00:14:02.210
is not that you have been
part of as many social

00:14:02.210 --> 00:14:04.630
organizations as possible,
where maybe you supported

00:14:04.630 --> 00:14:06.770
an event or did some minor activities,

00:14:06.770 --> 00:14:09.300
similar to the work experience
what you should really

00:14:09.300 --> 00:14:11.900
highlight and focus on here is the impact

00:14:11.900 --> 00:14:12.733
that you had.

00:14:12.733 --> 00:14:15.430
It's your leadership
in such an organization

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.090
that will make you really stand out.

00:14:17.090 --> 00:14:19.050
So I'd say it's completely okay to mention

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:21.580
three positions under
extracurriculars, I believe it's also

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:23.200
completely fine to only mention two,

00:14:23.200 --> 00:14:26.590
but then focus much more
on mentioning the specific

00:14:26.590 --> 00:14:27.780
things that you did.

00:14:27.780 --> 00:14:30.520
And again, quantify, so if
you organized the conference,

00:14:30.520 --> 00:14:32.650
say how many people
attended the conference,

00:14:32.650 --> 00:14:34.930
if you organized a
fundraiser, say what amount

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:36.200
of funds you raised.

00:14:36.200 --> 00:14:38.560
If you're the head of some
kind of social organization,

00:14:38.560 --> 00:14:41.000
say how many people you
are responsible for,

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.330
how many members this organization has.

00:14:43.330 --> 00:14:45.370
This is what's impressive,
this is how you show

00:14:45.370 --> 00:14:47.867
your leadership skills,
and volunteering in the end

00:14:47.867 --> 00:14:50.130
should be about the impact that you had,

00:14:50.130 --> 00:14:52.130
so make sure that you mention this impact

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:53.740
as precisely as possible.

00:14:53.740 --> 00:14:55.770
Now to the achievements
section here again I believe

00:14:55.770 --> 00:14:57.690
you can put this much more concisely.

00:14:57.690 --> 00:15:00.170
In general I do not believe
that it is necessary

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:02.840
to put the dates for
scholarships that you have.

00:15:02.840 --> 00:15:05.810
Nobody will care when exactly
you had a scholarship,

00:15:05.810 --> 00:15:07.810
of course if you then
submit all the supporting

00:15:07.810 --> 00:15:09.800
documents with your application
then you should also

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.690
have references for all your scholarships,

00:15:11.690 --> 00:15:13.430
and then these details
will be listed there

00:15:13.430 --> 00:15:14.510
if anybody's interested.

00:15:14.510 --> 00:15:16.700
But in general nobody
will care about that.

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:18.750
So no need to put the
dates, and instead of that,

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.610
again, I would just have one
line with your scholarships

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:23.400
and then just list all the scholarships

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:24.510
that you have collected.

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:26.060
This is hugely much more effective,

00:15:26.060 --> 00:15:27.287
and you can save lots of space for that.

00:15:27.287 --> 00:15:29.480
And similar things too,
for the publications,

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:31.540
so in general if you have
a background in academia,

00:15:31.540 --> 00:15:34.320
maybe you did a PhD and have
all kinds of publications,

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:37.370
then what you can do is
make an appendix to your CV

00:15:37.370 --> 00:15:38.980
listing all the publications.

00:15:38.980 --> 00:15:41.190
So what you can do here,
instead of now listing

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:43.860
the full citation of your paper, is again

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:46.350
in the achievements
section to have one remark,

00:15:46.350 --> 00:15:48.130
just briefly mention that
you have a publication,

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.520
the XYZ Journal, and then if
the journal is well rated,

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:54.540
so if the journal has I'd
say at least a B rating,

00:15:54.540 --> 00:15:57.850
or an A rating, or ideally
of course an A plus rating,

00:15:57.850 --> 00:16:00.090
then rather say how the journal is rated

00:16:00.090 --> 00:16:02.440
because this is what's really impressive,

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:04.600
in the end it's not
impressive to have a journal

00:16:04.600 --> 00:16:06.340
publication in a
completely unknown journal,

00:16:06.340 --> 00:16:08.940
but it is of course extremely
impressive if you have

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:10.490
an A plus publication.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:13.220
So rather talk about this
than spending all this space

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:16.060
on giving the full citation
of your journal paper,

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:17.670
somebody is really interested in that

00:16:17.670 --> 00:16:19.000
he can look it up anyways.

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:21.820
Okay, first one done, let's
jump into the next CV.

00:16:21.820 --> 00:16:24.500
And I'll try not to not
repeat myself too much,

00:16:24.500 --> 00:16:26.540
so I will not stress every single point

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.027
in the same way that I now I already did.

00:16:28.027 --> 00:16:30.030
But of course if you hear or see something

00:16:30.030 --> 00:16:32.377
that I already gave feedback
on in the earlier CVs

00:16:32.377 --> 00:16:34.710
the feedback will be
applicable here as well.

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:36.740
And this lady provided me some questions

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:38.260
that she asked me on her CV,

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:39.950
so I will now go over these questions

00:16:39.950 --> 00:16:41.750
and answer them, and by that I hope touch

00:16:41.750 --> 00:16:42.747
all the relevant points here.

00:16:42.747 --> 00:16:44.870
And the first question is
whether she should keep

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:47.250
the one-pager CV because
she feels like the CV

00:16:47.250 --> 00:16:49.620
is far too full, more
than enough stuff going on

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:51.070
to spread it out into two pages.

00:16:51.070 --> 00:16:52.697
And by now I hope the
answer is no surprise

00:16:52.697 --> 00:16:55.220
to you that no, you should
keep the one-pager format,

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:57.200
this at least would be
my strong recommendation.

00:16:57.200 --> 00:16:59.140
And I have no doubt at
all that you can fit

00:16:59.140 --> 00:17:02.010
all this information
easily on a one-pager CV.

00:17:02.010 --> 00:17:04.370
Because now the second
question was what I think

00:17:04.370 --> 00:17:07.007
about her layout, what you
directly see of course,

00:17:07.007 --> 00:17:09.490
this is a bit of an unorthodox layout.

00:17:09.490 --> 00:17:11.810
This is not the classical investment style

00:17:11.810 --> 00:17:13.920
one-pager CV that you see out there.

00:17:13.920 --> 00:17:17.220
And my general advice here
would be to be careful

00:17:17.220 --> 00:17:18.550
with these kind of things.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:21.240
So while of course I wouldn't
say that it looks bad

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:24.060
or something like that, you
should very carefully look out

00:17:24.060 --> 00:17:26.490
for the types of jobs that you apply for.

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:27.820
Especially if you apply for consulting

00:17:27.820 --> 00:17:31.550
or for investment banking,
these companies are a bit

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.420
conservative, and having
such an alternative design

00:17:34.420 --> 00:17:37.360
approach for your CV will
at least not help you

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:38.220
in the process.

00:17:38.220 --> 00:17:40.910
So I'm pretty sure that
nobody in the HR department

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:43.077
of Goldman Sachs, BCG or McKinsey
or wherever, will say,

00:17:43.077 --> 00:17:45.330
"Wow, this layout looks so great,"

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:46.910
this is just not how it works.

00:17:46.910 --> 00:17:49.350
So best case, people
will be just indifferent,

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:51.180
but of course worst
case will be that people

00:17:51.180 --> 00:17:52.690
are actually irritated by that.

00:17:52.690 --> 00:17:54.060
Now what could go through the head

00:17:54.060 --> 00:17:56.840
of an HR person is that this
candidate potentially just

00:17:56.840 --> 00:17:57.950
didn't do her research.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:01.290
This candidate just doesn't
know how a CV should look like

00:18:01.290 --> 00:18:02.880
in such a professional environment.

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:05.270
And this of course is not
the reaction that you want

00:18:05.270 --> 00:18:06.540
when you apply to these firms.

00:18:06.540 --> 00:18:08.730
So where I might see this a
bit differently is if you apply

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:09.970
for a creative position.

00:18:09.970 --> 00:18:13.015
If you apply for a marketing
agency, or any other job

00:18:13.015 --> 00:18:15.860
where creativity and
open mindedness is really

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:17.770
at the core of the job description.

00:18:17.770 --> 00:18:19.620
So for these kinds of
positions, yes, I believe

00:18:19.620 --> 00:18:21.980
it might be a great idea
to be a bit more creative,

00:18:21.980 --> 00:18:23.860
to think a bit more out
of the box regarding

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:25.487
the layout and the style of your CV,

00:18:25.487 --> 00:18:27.870
but of course this is
now a very specific field

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:28.703
that we are looking at.

00:18:28.703 --> 00:18:31.220
So my overall opinion on
that is that there isn't much

00:18:31.220 --> 00:18:33.960
of a upside of using
these kind of alternative

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:36.440
CV formats, but there is
the downside that somebody

00:18:36.440 --> 00:18:37.870
significantly dislikes this

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:39.210
and believes it's unprofessional.

00:18:39.210 --> 00:18:40.790
So I would just recommend not doing that

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:43.140
and rather going for a standard CV format.

00:18:43.140 --> 00:18:45.420
You want to impress by
the content of your CV

00:18:45.420 --> 00:18:46.710
and not by the layout.

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:48.720
Another thing I dislike about the layout

00:18:48.720 --> 00:18:52.070
that optically the focus of
this is here on the left part,

00:18:52.070 --> 00:18:53.400
there's the highlight.

00:18:53.400 --> 00:18:55.270
So I would claim that this left section

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:57.420
is rather the stuff that
you usually would put

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:00.070
in the footer of your
CV, so it's not actually

00:19:00.070 --> 00:19:03.160
the stuff that is really at
the core of what the viewer

00:19:03.160 --> 00:19:04.110
should be interested in.

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:06.610
But the most important stuff
is rather on the right.

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:08.610
So I do not think that
you're doing yourself a favor

00:19:08.610 --> 00:19:10.960
by setting it up this way,
by highlighting the things

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:12.790
that are less important for the viewer.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:14.600
Another thing that I'm
noticing, at least if I see it

00:19:14.600 --> 00:19:17.070
correctly, is that the
font size on the right

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:19.810
is smaller than the font size on the left.

00:19:19.810 --> 00:19:22.180
And to me this just doesn't
make sense for the one reason

00:19:22.180 --> 00:19:23.820
again that the stuff on
the right is actually

00:19:23.820 --> 00:19:25.720
more important than the stuff on the left,

00:19:25.720 --> 00:19:28.860
but also I believe that
it's in general bad practice

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:31.097
to use different font sizes in your CV.

00:19:31.097 --> 00:19:34.020
The only exception might be
maybe the name and the header

00:19:34.020 --> 00:19:36.700
which you maybe can do in a
bit of a higher font size,

00:19:36.700 --> 00:19:39.200
but even this is not
necessary, and for sure within

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:41.700
the body of your CV you
shouldn't work with different

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:44.120
font sizes, this is just
confusing to the eye.

00:19:44.120 --> 00:19:46.450
And another general remark
for your date ranges,

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:48.450
make sure that the orders of your elements

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:49.380
follows a logic.

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:52.100
And usually you start by the
things that are still ongoing,

00:19:52.100 --> 00:19:54.720
then you order the other
elements anti-chronologically

00:19:54.720 --> 00:19:57.220
when they have been completed,
or when this episode

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:58.060
has been finished.

00:19:58.060 --> 00:19:59.720
But this is now not the case here,

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:01.330
because if it is the case that the things

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:03.900
that are still ongoing are
put first, then why is this

00:20:03.900 --> 00:20:06.230
element this going on since November 16

00:20:06.230 --> 00:20:07.510
there at the bottom?

00:20:07.510 --> 00:20:09.680
Why isn't it above the TEDx element

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:10.720
if it's still ongoing?

00:20:10.720 --> 00:20:12.840
So the order of the elements
here just doesn't make sense

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:14.990
to me, make sure that yours do.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:16.760
And some other questions
that this lady had

00:20:16.760 --> 00:20:18.560
is first what can I take out?

00:20:18.560 --> 00:20:21.760
And second what do I do with
all these online courses

00:20:21.760 --> 00:20:22.593
that I took?

00:20:22.593 --> 00:20:24.170
So let's start with these online courses,

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:26.010
let's start with your education section.

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:28.090
Because I agree that the
way that this education

00:20:28.090 --> 00:20:30.800
section is setup at the
moment is pretty confusing.

00:20:30.800 --> 00:20:32.263
There's just so many elements in there,

00:20:32.263 --> 00:20:35.140
and you really need to pay
close attention til you really

00:20:35.140 --> 00:20:37.060
understand what your actual degrees are

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:38.830
and what some other study activities were,

00:20:38.830 --> 00:20:41.400
for instance these online
courses that you did in parallel.

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:43.780
My general advice here
would be that I wouldn't put

00:20:43.780 --> 00:20:46.980
online courses at the same
level as your full university

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:49.810
degrees, rather have this
footer section of your CV,

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:53.210
this other qualifications
section, and there you can then

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:55.440
list all your online courses,
and you shouldn't have

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:58.350
more than one line for each online course

00:20:58.350 --> 00:20:59.183
that you took.

00:20:59.183 --> 00:21:01.140
This will save you
significant space here above,

00:21:01.140 --> 00:21:03.870
and also will make it much
easier to read and much easier

00:21:03.870 --> 00:21:06.570
to process what exactly
you did, what exactly

00:21:06.570 --> 00:21:08.490
your main education and background is,

00:21:08.490 --> 00:21:11.150
because of course at least
today how HR departments

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:13.940
see that, this still your
university education,

00:21:13.940 --> 00:21:15.900
and less some online
courses that you took.

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:18.480
And similar thing holds
true for this project study

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:20.760
from 16, so if I understand
this correctly this lady

00:21:20.760 --> 00:21:22.970
took some university level
courses while she was

00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:25.210
still in high school, while
this is of course pretty cool

00:21:25.210 --> 00:21:28.070
I'd also not highlight this
here in the education section.

00:21:28.070 --> 00:21:30.650
I'd probably rather frame it
for something to be included

00:21:30.650 --> 00:21:32.680
in an honors and awards section.

00:21:32.680 --> 00:21:34.580
You can frame it as an academic honor

00:21:34.580 --> 00:21:36.700
that even though you
were only in high school

00:21:36.700 --> 00:21:38.510
the university already accepted you

00:21:38.510 --> 00:21:40.190
for a university level course.

00:21:40.190 --> 00:21:41.897
So I'd probably write something like this,

00:21:41.897 --> 00:21:44.870
"Admitted to the XYZ
Project," and then briefly

00:21:44.870 --> 00:21:45.947
describing it afterwards.

00:21:45.947 --> 00:21:48.070
And by doing that you can
really save some space

00:21:48.070 --> 00:21:49.380
here on the main section of your CV

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:52.470
where you should really
highlight the main stages

00:21:52.470 --> 00:21:53.860
of your academic career.

00:21:53.860 --> 00:21:55.750
The next question was
how she should handle

00:21:55.750 --> 00:21:58.330
her scholarships section,
what scholarships to include

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.730
and how to put it on the CV.

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:01.750
And again if you follow my basic template

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:03.580
then you have section honors and awards,

00:22:03.580 --> 00:22:05.110
and this is the section
where you can place

00:22:05.110 --> 00:22:06.200
all your scholarships.

00:22:06.200 --> 00:22:08.253
And now to what scholarship
exactly you should include,

00:22:08.253 --> 00:22:10.350
well something like the
Fulbright, of course,

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:12.540
is a very prestigious and
well known scholarship,

00:22:12.540 --> 00:22:15.000
so yes this for sure is something
that you should include.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:17.530
Now something like the
FemTec here, I do not know

00:22:17.530 --> 00:22:19.700
what exactly this is,
but sounds good, why not?

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:21.228
I mean, sure, sure you can include this.

00:22:21.228 --> 00:22:23.470
Now to one thing where there
are many questions around

00:22:23.470 --> 00:22:25.170
is this e-fellows scholarship.

00:22:25.170 --> 00:22:27.130
So this is a scholarship that is pretty

00:22:27.130 --> 00:22:29.250
well spread in Germany,
it's something that quite

00:22:29.250 --> 00:22:32.340
a lot of people have, but
of course not everybody has,

00:22:32.340 --> 00:22:34.600
so people ask themselves,
well should I include

00:22:34.600 --> 00:22:36.237
my e-fellows scholarship or not?

00:22:36.237 --> 00:22:39.120
And my simple answer would
be that probably I would

00:22:39.120 --> 00:22:41.220
include it if I have
nothing better to show.

00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:43.290
So again, looking at Germany,
once you have collected

00:22:43.290 --> 00:22:44.862
a BMBF scholarship, something like

00:22:44.862 --> 00:22:46.530
(speaking foreign language),
or something like that,

00:22:46.530 --> 00:22:48.280
then for sure I wouldn't
mention it anymore,

00:22:48.280 --> 00:22:49.960
but if your section on honors and awards

00:22:49.960 --> 00:22:51.870
still looks a bit empty
then yes, sure, why not?

00:22:51.870 --> 00:22:52.842
Then just include it.

00:22:52.842 --> 00:22:55.240
And this is now a general
point that I also said earlier,

00:22:55.240 --> 00:22:57.680
what exactly you will
include or not include

00:22:57.680 --> 00:23:00.370
on your CV depends on
what stage of your career,

00:23:00.370 --> 00:23:03.160
what stage also of your university
study program you're at.

00:23:03.160 --> 00:23:05.320
In the beginning if you're
fresh out of high school,

00:23:05.320 --> 00:23:07.590
if you are in the first
semesters of your university

00:23:07.590 --> 00:23:09.930
program, then it's completely
okay to also include

00:23:09.930 --> 00:23:11.510
for instance internships that you did

00:23:11.510 --> 00:23:13.680
during your high school
time, which maybe were only

00:23:13.680 --> 00:23:16.350
a couple of weeks long, but
over time, once you did more

00:23:16.350 --> 00:23:18.700
relevant internships, more
prestigious internships,

00:23:18.700 --> 00:23:21.060
then at some point take
this older stuff out.

00:23:21.060 --> 00:23:24.100
In my opinion you are
strongly devaluing your strong

00:23:24.100 --> 00:23:26.210
internships if they stand next to this

00:23:26.210 --> 00:23:28.740
high school thing you did for two weeks,

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:30.660
some where where you were
a really young person.

00:23:30.660 --> 00:23:32.650
And same thing is true
here for the scholarships,

00:23:32.650 --> 00:23:35.060
I would leave it in until I
have enough other academic

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:36.710
honors and awards that then at some point

00:23:36.710 --> 00:23:38.830
can replace this e-fellows scholarship.

00:23:38.830 --> 00:23:40.890
Now regarding the
content, how you describe

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:43.030
your work experience,
this is really an area

00:23:43.030 --> 00:23:45.320
of your CV where I would
highly recommend you to go

00:23:45.320 --> 00:23:46.170
over that again.

00:23:46.170 --> 00:23:48.240
Now I do not want to
repeat all things I said

00:23:48.240 --> 00:23:50.450
for the previous CV, but
it's really important

00:23:50.450 --> 00:23:53.940
that you focus much more
on your contribution,

00:23:53.940 --> 00:23:56.390
on the impact that you had while working

00:23:56.390 --> 00:23:57.223
in these positions.

00:23:57.223 --> 00:24:00.070
And again, quantify, always quantify,

00:24:00.070 --> 00:24:03.540
try to have a number in almost
every single bullet point

00:24:03.540 --> 00:24:06.100
that you use when describing
your work experience,

00:24:06.100 --> 00:24:08.430
and similar thing, actually,
is true for your volunteering,

00:24:08.430 --> 00:24:10.247
for your extracurricular
experience as well.

00:24:10.247 --> 00:24:12.780
And now to your volunteering
section, here you list

00:24:12.780 --> 00:24:16.120
five different activities,
most of them also overlap.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.633
As somebody who reads the
CV I would probably doubt

00:24:18.633 --> 00:24:21.970
that you were really able
to have a significant impact

00:24:21.970 --> 00:24:24.470
in all these positions, so what
I would really recommend you

00:24:24.470 --> 00:24:27.780
is to focus more, maybe instead
of mentioning five things,

00:24:27.780 --> 00:24:30.380
rather cut it down to
the three or so things

00:24:30.380 --> 00:24:32.580
that you really feel like
were the most important,

00:24:32.580 --> 00:24:33.777
most relevant to you.

00:24:33.777 --> 00:24:36.530
And here again now focus
on your leadership,

00:24:36.530 --> 00:24:40.580
on your impact, what you did
to really make a contribution,

00:24:40.580 --> 00:24:42.530
make an impact to your community.

00:24:42.530 --> 00:24:44.340
This is what your extracurricular section

00:24:44.340 --> 00:24:46.770
should be all about, how
you made a contribution

00:24:46.770 --> 00:24:48.030
for the good of society.

00:24:48.030 --> 00:24:49.290
Now to the next CV.

00:24:49.290 --> 00:24:51.150
What I want to point
out in the beginning is

00:24:51.150 --> 00:24:53.940
that without reading a single
word, just from the look

00:24:53.940 --> 00:24:56.700
and feel of that, this is how a classical

00:24:56.700 --> 00:24:59.250
Anglo-Saxon one-pager CV looks like.

00:24:59.250 --> 00:25:00.860
So if you wonder what a
good and sorted layout

00:25:00.860 --> 00:25:04.220
of an MBB consulting, of
an investment banking CV

00:25:04.220 --> 00:25:07.080
looks like, this is the look
and feel that you wanna go for.

00:25:07.080 --> 00:25:09.180
Maybe some of you believe
that it's too full,

00:25:09.180 --> 00:25:11.160
that it's too packed with content,

00:25:11.160 --> 00:25:13.190
but what you need to
understand is that the feeling

00:25:13.190 --> 00:25:14.960
that you wanna create, the look and feel,

00:25:14.960 --> 00:25:17.240
needs to be that it's completely packed

00:25:17.240 --> 00:25:18.870
with amazingness of yourself.

00:25:18.870 --> 00:25:20.660
This is the picture
that you wanna portray.

00:25:20.660 --> 00:25:23.960
So somebody who reads the
CV, you wanna just go over it

00:25:23.960 --> 00:25:27.190
and read every single
line, and every single line

00:25:27.190 --> 00:25:29.880
is just impressive,
great university names,

00:25:29.880 --> 00:25:31.990
great grades, great accomplishments,

00:25:31.990 --> 00:25:35.010
great impact, great
numbers, this is the feeling

00:25:35.010 --> 00:25:35.870
that you wanna go for.

00:25:35.870 --> 00:25:37.590
What you also see here is that in contrast

00:25:37.590 --> 00:25:40.250
to all the other CVs he
has very little margins

00:25:40.250 --> 00:25:42.600
at the side, at the
top, and at the bottom.

00:25:42.600 --> 00:25:45.087
Again, this is very typical
for these kinds of CVs,

00:25:45.087 --> 00:25:47.160
'cause this really
allows you to just stuff

00:25:47.160 --> 00:25:48.500
lots of content into them.

00:25:48.500 --> 00:25:50.387
This guy is currently
an LSE master student

00:25:50.387 --> 00:25:52.190
and he told me that he already worked with

00:25:52.190 --> 00:25:54.580
the career services at LSE on his CV,

00:25:54.580 --> 00:25:55.760
and you can really see that.

00:25:55.760 --> 00:25:57.480
At least for these high profile consulting

00:25:57.480 --> 00:25:59.120
and banking jobs, this is the style

00:25:59.120 --> 00:25:59.953
that you should go for.

00:25:59.953 --> 00:26:01.720
Another thing that I'd
also like to point out

00:26:01.720 --> 00:26:04.350
is how little space he
is using in the header

00:26:04.350 --> 00:26:06.310
to put all his contact information.

00:26:06.310 --> 00:26:08.840
If you look at the other CVs,
there the contact information

00:26:08.840 --> 00:26:11.790
take a quarter, or even
a third of the page.

00:26:11.790 --> 00:26:14.100
This is just a complete waste of space.

00:26:14.100 --> 00:26:16.970
You can just have that in two
lines or so in the header,

00:26:16.970 --> 00:26:18.100
and this is completely fine.

00:26:18.100 --> 00:26:19.860
So even though this is
already looking great,

00:26:19.860 --> 00:26:21.620
I do believe there are a couple of things

00:26:21.620 --> 00:26:23.540
he can do to make this even stronger.

00:26:23.540 --> 00:26:25.460
One thing is that at least in my opinion

00:26:25.460 --> 00:26:27.580
he did a bit too much on the formatting.

00:26:27.580 --> 00:26:30.430
So he uses capitalization, he uses bold,

00:26:30.430 --> 00:26:32.830
he uses italic, he uses underlines.

00:26:32.830 --> 00:26:34.687
Individually this is
okay but I wouldn't do

00:26:34.687 --> 00:26:36.080
all these things at the same time.

00:26:36.080 --> 00:26:38.380
So probably for instance
here I wouldn't work also

00:26:38.380 --> 00:26:39.620
with italic font.

00:26:39.620 --> 00:26:42.000
If almost everything in
your CV is highlighted

00:26:42.000 --> 00:26:44.700
by capitalization,
boldness, italic, underlines

00:26:44.700 --> 00:26:47.410
and so on, this loses meaning,
and these kind of highlights

00:26:47.410 --> 00:26:49.110
you want to use to create a structure

00:26:49.110 --> 00:26:51.270
on your CV, so I'd probably
just take one step back

00:26:51.270 --> 00:26:53.430
and probably take out for
instance the italic font.

00:26:53.430 --> 00:26:55.080
The next thing is that
even though, as I said,

00:26:55.080 --> 00:26:57.540
it's great to really pack
it with lots of content,

00:26:57.540 --> 00:27:00.120
you should make sure that
it's easy to understand

00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:02.010
when the new entries starts.

00:27:02.010 --> 00:27:04.750
Here I believe that the
distance between two entries

00:27:04.750 --> 00:27:07.660
is almost the same as the
distance between two lines

00:27:07.660 --> 00:27:08.630
within one entry.

00:27:08.630 --> 00:27:11.870
So I would change that and
I would slightly increase

00:27:11.870 --> 00:27:15.040
the distance between two
entries to make it easier

00:27:15.040 --> 00:27:16.970
to read when a new entry begins.

00:27:16.970 --> 00:27:18.610
And yes, this is taking some space,

00:27:18.610 --> 00:27:20.670
but in a few moments I will
also give you a bit more

00:27:20.670 --> 00:27:23.120
suggestions on what you can
do to save some more space.

00:27:23.120 --> 00:27:25.150
So let's now jump into
the education section.

00:27:25.150 --> 00:27:26.830
The first remark that I wanna make here

00:27:26.830 --> 00:27:28.920
is how you state foreign grades.

00:27:28.920 --> 00:27:31.630
So this is now a CV in English,
but he studied in Germany

00:27:31.630 --> 00:27:32.463
in his undergraduate.

00:27:32.463 --> 00:27:34.500
And then what some people
do, as in this example,

00:27:34.500 --> 00:27:36.850
is that they take their
German grade and then they try

00:27:36.850 --> 00:27:39.600
to calculate that into
some other kind of format,

00:27:39.600 --> 00:27:42.784
and here this example onto
the American format of 4.0.

00:27:42.784 --> 00:27:44.750
And here the general rule
is that you should not

00:27:44.750 --> 00:27:45.840
tamper with your grades.

00:27:45.840 --> 00:27:47.640
You shouldn't by your
own initiative now try

00:27:47.640 --> 00:27:50.290
to apply some kind of calculation formula

00:27:50.290 --> 00:27:53.310
to transfer it in any kind
of other grade system.

00:27:53.310 --> 00:27:55.860
You should always state the
grade exactly in the way

00:27:55.860 --> 00:27:58.870
that it is stated in your
diploma that you received.

00:27:58.870 --> 00:28:01.630
So of course now if you did
receive a diploma in English

00:28:01.630 --> 00:28:03.560
and it showed the grade
in exactly this way,

00:28:03.560 --> 00:28:05.910
then it is fine, but in
general I would not do

00:28:05.910 --> 00:28:07.760
these kind of calculations by yourself.

00:28:07.760 --> 00:28:10.130
Same true is here for this
German School of Milan

00:28:10.130 --> 00:28:12.070
for the 98 out of 100 scale.

00:28:12.070 --> 00:28:14.470
So of course if you received
a diploma where the grade

00:28:14.470 --> 00:28:16.727
is stated this way, then
I would put it this way,

00:28:16.727 --> 00:28:19.530
but I wouldn't do these kind
of calculations by yourself.

00:28:19.530 --> 00:28:22.110
Now just a minor remark on
the bullet with the poli sci

00:28:22.110 --> 00:28:24.620
program here, there seems
to be a double spacing,

00:28:24.620 --> 00:28:26.420
so just take out one of the spaces.

00:28:26.420 --> 00:28:29.500
Regarding this Brown
University pre-college program,

00:28:29.500 --> 00:28:31.630
this is likely something
where you can save a bit

00:28:31.630 --> 00:28:34.570
more space, I would probably
not put this as prominently

00:28:34.570 --> 00:28:36.470
here in your main education section,

00:28:36.470 --> 00:28:39.100
but for me this is rather
something you can put below

00:28:39.100 --> 00:28:40.590
under other qualifications.

00:28:40.590 --> 00:28:42.770
And the reason is that even
though Brown University

00:28:42.770 --> 00:28:45.420
of course sounds great, it's
a great Ivy League university,

00:28:45.420 --> 00:28:47.640
you usually do not get admitted
to these kind of summer

00:28:47.640 --> 00:28:49.890
school programs due to
your academic merit,

00:28:49.890 --> 00:28:52.820
but usually you just pay for
it, and everybody knows that,

00:28:52.820 --> 00:28:54.560
so I wouldn't consider
this now a great academic

00:28:54.560 --> 00:28:56.690
achievement, but rather put it below under

00:28:56.690 --> 00:28:58.500
other qualifications where
you can just state it

00:28:58.500 --> 00:29:00.780
in one line or so and thereby save space.

00:29:00.780 --> 00:29:03.210
Now regarding the content
here again, I just wanna

00:29:03.210 --> 00:29:06.590
encourage you to focus much
more on your contribution,

00:29:06.590 --> 00:29:07.530
on your impact.

00:29:07.530 --> 00:29:09.980
Just as an example in
your childcare position

00:29:09.980 --> 00:29:11.960
you write that you
developed teaching plans

00:29:11.960 --> 00:29:13.330
and that you taught children.

00:29:13.330 --> 00:29:14.980
Here I would really quantify this now,

00:29:14.980 --> 00:29:18.130
for instance by saying that
you taught 200 students

00:29:18.130 --> 00:29:20.010
in total, or by saying
that you taught three

00:29:20.010 --> 00:29:22.760
different classes of students,
or anything like that.

00:29:22.760 --> 00:29:24.477
This just makes it much more tangible

00:29:24.477 --> 00:29:26.890
and really shows that
you made this impact,

00:29:26.890 --> 00:29:28.230
that you were the teacher.

00:29:28.230 --> 00:29:31.450
Really always stress much
more on your contribution,

00:29:31.450 --> 00:29:32.760
the impact that you had.

00:29:32.760 --> 00:29:34.530
And on the next point,
the fundraiser point,

00:29:34.530 --> 00:29:36.710
the guy asked me whether he should include

00:29:36.710 --> 00:29:39.880
now the quantification of
$1,000, because he feels

00:29:39.880 --> 00:29:41.910
like maybe this is a
bit little of an amount

00:29:41.910 --> 00:29:42.743
to mention that.

00:29:42.743 --> 00:29:44.840
And at least in my opinion,
again, even though it's not

00:29:44.840 --> 00:29:47.470
the largest amount, I believe
it's much more honest,

00:29:47.470 --> 00:29:50.070
it's much more tangible to
write that you raised $1,000

00:29:50.070 --> 00:29:51.270
than to not writing that.

00:29:51.270 --> 00:29:53.080
Personally believe that
this is the better thing

00:29:53.080 --> 00:29:54.300
to do, and that this is the thing

00:29:54.300 --> 00:29:55.670
that is just more powerful.

00:29:55.670 --> 00:29:56.710
Hi guys, Heinrich here.

00:29:56.710 --> 00:29:58.690
So while editing I noticed that somehow

00:29:58.690 --> 00:30:00.243
a part of the video was missing.

00:30:00.243 --> 00:30:03.230
And now the next session
refers to a question

00:30:03.230 --> 00:30:05.400
this guy asked me, and
he asked me two questions

00:30:05.400 --> 00:30:08.530
specifically, first how
important is it really

00:30:08.530 --> 00:30:10.990
to quantify all your achievements?

00:30:10.990 --> 00:30:14.230
And second, is it okay
to exaggerate in your CV?

00:30:14.230 --> 00:30:16.930
To what extent can you maybe inflate a bit

00:30:16.930 --> 00:30:19.190
the things that you did,
and what is the line

00:30:19.190 --> 00:30:20.170
that you should not cross?

00:30:20.170 --> 00:30:21.930
So now the next section refers to.

00:30:21.930 --> 00:30:24.560
Yes, quantification is great,
it just helps you to make

00:30:24.560 --> 00:30:27.140
the things that you did
sound much more tangible

00:30:27.140 --> 00:30:29.670
and really helps to tear out the impact

00:30:29.670 --> 00:30:31.100
that you had in your roles.

00:30:31.100 --> 00:30:33.320
So to what level is it okay to exaggerate?

00:30:33.320 --> 00:30:35.080
And here I'd make the remark that yes,

00:30:35.080 --> 00:30:37.730
it's true, that probably
most of the CVs that you get

00:30:37.730 --> 00:30:40.560
in your hand, there's some
level of exaggeration in it,

00:30:40.560 --> 00:30:42.660
of course people try to portray themselves

00:30:42.660 --> 00:30:45.760
as positively as possible,
so because your competition

00:30:45.760 --> 00:30:48.140
is doing you should of course not be shy.

00:30:48.140 --> 00:30:50.550
Make sure that you at least
state all the achievements

00:30:50.550 --> 00:30:52.840
in the appropriate level of greatness.

00:30:52.840 --> 00:30:55.260
Do not hold back, really make it salient

00:30:55.260 --> 00:30:56.820
what the impact is that you had,

00:30:56.820 --> 00:30:58.430
what the leadership is that you showed,

00:30:58.430 --> 00:31:00.420
do not be modest here in your CV,

00:31:00.420 --> 00:31:01.607
this is not what will help you.

00:31:01.607 --> 00:31:04.100
But of course there is
a limit, and this limit

00:31:04.100 --> 00:31:07.130
is where you're now making
factually wrong statements.

00:31:07.130 --> 00:31:08.860
This for me is now an ethics issue.

00:31:08.860 --> 00:31:11.490
While I'm sure that many,
many people exaggerate

00:31:11.490 --> 00:31:13.300
the things that they write on their CV,

00:31:13.300 --> 00:31:15.850
even beyond what's
actually factually true,

00:31:15.850 --> 00:31:17.600
in my opinion this is just unethical

00:31:17.600 --> 00:31:19.600
and I just would not cross this line.

00:31:19.600 --> 00:31:21.830
This will probably put you
at a slight disadvantage

00:31:21.830 --> 00:31:23.483
compared to some other
candidates, but hey,

00:31:23.483 --> 00:31:24.410
life is unfair.

00:31:24.410 --> 00:31:26.930
So now last but not least, CV number four.

00:31:26.930 --> 00:31:28.580
This is now again a two page CV,

00:31:28.580 --> 00:31:30.210
and here again I would
of course recommend you

00:31:30.210 --> 00:31:33.210
to put it on one page, especially
because the second page

00:31:33.210 --> 00:31:34.210
is barely used.

00:31:34.210 --> 00:31:36.760
So here it would be especially
easy for you to consolidate

00:31:36.760 --> 00:31:37.837
it all on one page,

00:31:37.837 --> 00:31:38.670
and this is something that therefore

00:31:38.670 --> 00:31:39.910
I would highly recommend.

00:31:39.910 --> 00:31:42.060
Next thing you notice is
that the header is missing

00:31:42.060 --> 00:31:44.020
with the contact information, so I assume

00:31:44.020 --> 00:31:45.910
he just took it out to anonymize himself,

00:31:45.910 --> 00:31:48.230
but of course in your
actual CV you should include

00:31:48.230 --> 00:31:49.697
a contact information section at the top.

00:31:49.697 --> 00:31:51.770
One thing that I like about this CV

00:31:51.770 --> 00:31:54.740
is how he put the dates, saying
this because I now referred

00:31:54.740 --> 00:31:57.770
to this earlier how he's using
these numbers for the months,

00:31:57.770 --> 00:31:59.200
and then the slash and then the year,

00:31:59.200 --> 00:32:01.470
I believe this is a very
clean and easy to read

00:32:01.470 --> 00:32:02.780
and easy to understand format.

00:32:02.780 --> 00:32:04.780
So at least for my taste,
this works quite well.

00:32:04.780 --> 00:32:07.440
Regarding the overall
layout, be a bit careful

00:32:07.440 --> 00:32:09.640
that everything is nicely aligned.

00:32:09.640 --> 00:32:11.910
So what you can see here
is that these blue lines

00:32:11.910 --> 00:32:15.650
they do not neatly start at
the very left of the letters,

00:32:15.650 --> 00:32:17.980
but rather a bit more to
the right, so this looks

00:32:17.980 --> 00:32:20.670
a bit unclean, this is
just not correctly aligned,

00:32:20.670 --> 00:32:22.230
so just have a look at that again, please.

00:32:22.230 --> 00:32:24.110
And the same is for the
indentation, so at least

00:32:24.110 --> 00:32:26.780
if I see this correctly,
at the left, the dates,

00:32:26.780 --> 00:32:29.100
they do not all begin
at the very same plane,

00:32:29.100 --> 00:32:31.140
so make sure that the
indentation is consistent

00:32:31.140 --> 00:32:33.220
and all the bullets
start at the same level.

00:32:33.220 --> 00:32:35.480
So what this guy did
very well is the GMAT.

00:32:35.480 --> 00:32:37.640
So usually I would recommend
to not put the GMAT

00:32:37.640 --> 00:32:40.780
above at the education
section, but maybe below

00:32:40.780 --> 00:32:42.800
in the honors, or maybe in
the other qualifications

00:32:42.800 --> 00:32:44.770
section, or somewhere below, but of course

00:32:44.770 --> 00:32:47.500
if you did a very strong
GMAT as this gentleman did,

00:32:47.500 --> 00:32:49.550
maybe especially then if
your other grades aren't

00:32:49.550 --> 00:32:51.940
that strong, then it is an
option that you could go for

00:32:51.940 --> 00:32:54.590
to then also include the
GMAT next to the degree

00:32:54.590 --> 00:32:56.260
that you took the GMAT for.

00:32:56.260 --> 00:32:59.240
Here of course the GMAT
of 740 is a very strong

00:32:59.240 --> 00:33:01.440
score that might very well overcompensate

00:33:01.440 --> 00:33:03.850
some other weaknesses in the
GPAs of the other degrees.

00:33:03.850 --> 00:33:06.050
Now because already I said
so much about how you should

00:33:06.050 --> 00:33:08.450
write your bullets in your
work experience section,

00:33:08.450 --> 00:33:10.510
let's rather look into the skills section

00:33:10.510 --> 00:33:12.210
because here he did something which I see

00:33:12.210 --> 00:33:14.370
many people do in some variations,

00:33:14.370 --> 00:33:15.523
which at least personally I believe

00:33:15.523 --> 00:33:16.960
that you should not do this.

00:33:16.960 --> 00:33:19.690
And this is this weird
scale that he is using

00:33:19.690 --> 00:33:21.850
to measure the level of his skills.

00:33:21.850 --> 00:33:23.880
And while first of all I
find it highly doubtful

00:33:23.880 --> 00:33:25.787
whether you should
include Microsoft Office

00:33:25.787 --> 00:33:29.080
skills in general on your
CV as I also said earlier,

00:33:29.080 --> 00:33:30.520
but let's now assume that you include it,

00:33:30.520 --> 00:33:33.740
where I would now be very, very careful

00:33:33.740 --> 00:33:36.810
is if you put yourself as a full expert

00:33:36.810 --> 00:33:39.700
on such a topic, six out of six points,

00:33:39.700 --> 00:33:43.190
so basically 100% proficient
user of this tool,

00:33:43.190 --> 00:33:45.260
and just to contrast
that, so I would consider

00:33:45.260 --> 00:33:48.160
myself a pretty proficient
user with for instance Excel

00:33:48.160 --> 00:33:50.760
as well, but I would
never claim that I'm at

00:33:50.760 --> 00:33:54.040
the 100%, that I know it all about a tool

00:33:54.040 --> 00:33:54.880
such as Excel.

00:33:54.880 --> 00:33:57.920
Because in Excel, even though
you're already quite advanced,

00:33:57.920 --> 00:33:59.810
there are always more topics to learn,

00:33:59.810 --> 00:34:03.390
more topics to master, let's
start with array formulas,

00:34:03.390 --> 00:34:07.400
with PowerPivot, with VBA,
all these very advanced

00:34:07.400 --> 00:34:10.640
techniques, and if you really
master all these things,

00:34:10.640 --> 00:34:12.920
if you're really an expert, then okay,

00:34:12.920 --> 00:34:14.367
then maybe at some point
you can write that.

00:34:14.367 --> 00:34:17.170
But just be careful here,
because as an interviewer,

00:34:17.170 --> 00:34:19.450
if I see this, I would
just directly pick it up

00:34:19.450 --> 00:34:21.077
and challenge the candidate a bit on that.

00:34:21.077 --> 00:34:24.320
And then also the Microsoft
Office suite is so vast

00:34:24.320 --> 00:34:27.350
besides these basic programs
like PowerPoint, Excel,

00:34:27.350 --> 00:34:30.230
or Word, it also includes
programs like SharePoint,

00:34:30.230 --> 00:34:33.700
or Access, and do you really
master all these tools

00:34:33.700 --> 00:34:35.620
at the 100% level?

00:34:35.620 --> 00:34:36.770
So guys, be careful.

00:34:36.770 --> 00:34:39.050
And similar things are true
for your language skills.

00:34:39.050 --> 00:34:42.773
So if you put languages on
your CV on the B1 level or so,

00:34:42.773 --> 00:34:45.550
then be ready that the
interviewer maybe in the middle

00:34:45.550 --> 00:34:48.400
of the interview switches to
Italian, or switches to French,

00:34:48.400 --> 00:34:50.340
just to test the bit
whether you do have these

00:34:50.340 --> 00:34:52.780
basic language skills
that you claim to have.

00:34:52.780 --> 00:34:54.940
So if you can speak these
languages at these levels,

00:34:54.940 --> 00:34:56.600
this is perfect, but
this is just something

00:34:56.600 --> 00:34:58.760
where it's really easy to call you out

00:34:58.760 --> 00:35:00.427
in an interview, so be careful.

00:35:00.427 --> 00:35:02.730
And the last thing I wanna
draw your attention to here

00:35:02.730 --> 00:35:04.600
on the activities section is hunting.

00:35:04.600 --> 00:35:06.610
And with hunting, it's a bit
similar to an affiliation

00:35:06.610 --> 00:35:09.030
to a political party, so
while I trust that it can be

00:35:09.030 --> 00:35:11.690
a very comforting leisure
activity, maybe also

00:35:11.690 --> 00:35:14.270
a great conversation starter,
if your interview partner

00:35:14.270 --> 00:35:17.030
is interested in that, or
maybe does the same activity,

00:35:17.030 --> 00:35:19.780
there just are people who
see things like hunting

00:35:19.780 --> 00:35:22.390
very critically, and some
of them are not really open

00:35:22.390 --> 00:35:24.480
for arguments, but rather see these things

00:35:24.480 --> 00:35:25.620
on an ideological level.

00:35:25.620 --> 00:35:27.840
So I would probably not write on my CV

00:35:27.840 --> 00:35:30.270
that I am a hunter, because
there might be some people

00:35:30.270 --> 00:35:33.100
in HR believing that
hunters are really evil

00:35:33.100 --> 00:35:35.930
and unmoral persons, and
by now I trust it's easy

00:35:35.930 --> 00:35:38.350
to make an argument in
the exact other direction,

00:35:38.350 --> 00:35:41.000
you just do not wanna put
your application at risk

00:35:41.000 --> 00:35:42.400
for such a stupid little thing.

00:35:42.400 --> 00:35:44.890
Okay, so let's wrap it
up, this was my review

00:35:44.890 --> 00:35:48.020
of your CVs, I hope that
you found this interesting

00:35:48.020 --> 00:35:50.097
and valuable, and I hope that
you really took something

00:35:50.097 --> 00:35:52.360
out for your individual CVs as well,

00:35:52.360 --> 00:35:54.900
that this really helped
you to get your application

00:35:54.900 --> 00:35:56.120
material to the next level.

00:35:56.120 --> 00:35:57.850
So now I'd love to hear also from you,

00:35:57.850 --> 00:35:59.900
what you have, other suggestions,

00:35:59.900 --> 00:36:02.340
other tips for the four
CVs that we looked at.

00:36:02.340 --> 00:36:04.300
Leave a comment below
in the comment section

00:36:04.300 --> 00:36:06.790
so that also the other
people here in the community

00:36:06.790 --> 00:36:08.360
can participate from your knowledge,

00:36:08.360 --> 00:36:09.810
I would highly appreciate that.

